The Japanese version above is authoritative. This English version is provided for reference only.

### 1. Definitions and Scope

“Software” means the Artifact Share software and associated documentation to which this license is attached, including `@artifactshare/qm-bridge` under `packages/qm-bridge/`.

“Licensor” means TechTalk, Inc. “You” means an individual or legal entity that obtains a copy of the Software and exercises rights under this license.

### 2. Permission Grant

Subject to the terms of this license, You are granted, free of charge, the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and sell the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do the same.

### 3. Preservation of Notices

The copyright notice above and the complete text of this license must be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

### 4. Restriction on Offering a Competing Service

You and downstream recipients must not offer the Software, including modified or derivative versions, to third parties as a hosted, managed, Software-as-a-Service, or cloud service that directly competes with the Licensor and whose primary value is the functionality of the Software itself. The permission to sublicense or sell under Section 2 does not grant a right to circumvent this restriction.

The following uses are not prohibited solely by this Section:

- self-hosting operated by an organization for its own business use;
- deployment and maintenance by a vendor in an environment dedicated to one customer, provided that the vendor does not itself offer a competing service to multiple customers; and
- incorporation into another product or service whose primary value is not the functionality of Artifact Share itself.

For a commercial license covering a use restricted by this Section, contact `support@artifactshare.com`.

### 5. Names and Trademarks

This license grants no rights in the Artifact Share name, logos, service marks, or other trademarks. You may use them only as necessary to describe origin accurately or to redistribute unmodified brand assets included with the Software together with the Software. You must not use them in a way that is likely to imply an official version, approval, affiliation, or sponsorship by the Licensor.

### 6. Proposals and Contributions

Contributors retain copyright in proposals and other submissions. A contributor grants the Licensor and the maintainers of the Software a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, sublicensable license to evaluate, accept, incorporate into the Software, modify, reproduce, publish, and distribute the submission.

This Section is not an invitation for code contributions at this time. If code contributions are accepted in the future, their inbound license terms and any contributor agreement will be stated separately.

### 7. Termination

Your rights under this license terminate if You violate its terms. If You cure all violations within 30 days after becoming aware of them, Your rights are automatically reinstated for the first violation. Reinstatement after an uncured or repeated violation requires the Licensor's written consent.

### 8. Disclaimer of Warranty

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS,” WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NONINFRINGEMENT.

### 9. Limitation of Liability

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE AUTHORS AND COPYRIGHT HOLDERS SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM OR RELATED TO THE SOFTWARE OR ITS USE OR OTHER DEALINGS. THIS LIMITATION DOES NOT APPLY TO LIABILITY THAT CANNOT BE EXCLUDED OR LIMITED UNDER MANDATORY APPLICABLE LAW.

### 10. Governing Law and Jurisdiction

